1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:07,924
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,969 --> 00:00:13,096
<i>Have you heard the news?</i>
<i>Someone from the co-op died.</i>

3
00:00:13,179 --> 00:00:14,139
<i>Yes. Mr. Ramon.</i>

4
00:00:14,222 --> 00:00:15,640
<i>With all the people you had killed,</i>

5
00:00:15,724 --> 00:00:17,434
<i>you might as well be the Grim Reaper.</i>

6
00:00:17,517 --> 00:00:20,353
<i>I only did what I had to do.</i>

7
00:00:20,437 --> 00:00:21,688
<i>You always make decisions</i>

8
00:00:21,771 --> 00:00:23,732
<i>without thinking of the consequences…</i>

9
00:00:23,815 --> 00:00:26,651
<i>so no wonder Grandpa</i>
<i>still can't trust you!</i>

10
00:00:26,735 --> 00:00:28,653
<i>I wish I wasn't born an Ardiente!</i>

11
00:00:28,737 --> 00:00:31,823
<i>I swear I won't come back here</i>
<i>until I prove</i>

12
00:00:31,906 --> 00:00:35,702
<i>you had a hand in Mr. Ramon's death</i>

13
00:00:35,785 --> 00:00:38,038
<i>and the other killings in this town!</i>

14
00:00:38,121 --> 00:00:39,748
<i>I just came here to offer my condolences</i>

15
00:00:39,831 --> 00:00:42,000
<i>and tell you the project is on hold.</i>

16
00:00:42,083 --> 00:00:43,293
<i>Did someone have to die first</i>

17
00:00:43,376 --> 00:00:45,545
<i>before you realize</i>
<i>what you're doing is wrong?</i>

18
00:00:45,628 --> 00:00:47,422
<i>-You monster!</i>
<i>-Mr. Dolfo!</i>

19
00:00:47,505 --> 00:00:48,590
<i>You monster!</i>

20
00:00:48,965 --> 00:00:50,842
<i>-Ivy, wait!</i>
<i>-You're concerned?</i>

21
00:00:50,925 --> 00:00:53,386
[Diego] <i>Do you think I'd ever</i>
<i>let you get hurt?</i>

22
00:00:53,470 --> 00:00:56,431
<i>What he did was wrong.</i>
<i>But, please, don't file charges.</i>

23
00:00:56,514 --> 00:00:57,390
[Ivy] <i>I didn't file charges.</i>

24
00:00:57,474 --> 00:00:59,350
<i>Please forgive me for what I did.</i>

25
00:00:59,434 --> 00:01:01,227
<i>I understand you.</i>

26
00:01:01,311 --> 00:01:03,521
<i>I know how you feel.</i>

27
00:01:03,605 --> 00:01:06,858
<i>I know the pain</i>
<i>of losing someone you love.</i>

28
00:01:06,941 --> 00:01:07,859
[Arnaldo] <i>I saw you two.</i>

29
00:01:07,942 --> 00:01:09,527
<i>Do you think I liked what you did?</i>

30
00:01:09,611 --> 00:01:10,862
<i>Ivy is mine.</i>

31
00:01:10,945 --> 00:01:13,573
<i>And if I see you</i>
<i>hovering around her again…</i>

32
00:01:13,656 --> 00:01:14,866
[clicks tongue]

33
00:01:14,949 --> 00:01:16,034
[Claire] <i>How is your father doing?</i>

34
00:01:16,117 --> 00:01:17,202
[Emilia] <i>I don't want to know.</i>

35
00:01:17,285 --> 00:01:19,329
[Claire] <i>Aren't you excited</i>
<i>for your father</i>

36
00:01:19,412 --> 00:01:21,122
<i>to return alive and limping?</i>

37
00:01:21,206 --> 00:01:23,124
[Emilia] <i>Not now. I'm only just starting.</i>

38
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:25,710
<i>He has Natalie, Dad!</i>
<i>Why does he even need Ivy?</i>

39
00:01:25,794 --> 00:01:26,878
<i>Why? Do you like Ivy, too?</i>

40
00:01:26,961 --> 00:01:28,671
[Diego] <i>I can't explain</i>
<i>what I feel for her,</i>

41
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:30,840
<i>but it feels like</i>
<i>I've known her for so long.</i>

42
00:01:30,924 --> 00:01:32,509
<i>I want to get to know her more.</i>

43
00:01:32,592 --> 00:01:34,803
<i>I want to protect her from Arnaldo.</i>

44
00:01:39,974 --> 00:01:45,021
[heart monitor beeping]

45
00:01:46,773 --> 00:01:53,530
[ominous music playing]

46
00:01:56,199 --> 00:01:59,619
[phone ringing]

47
00:02:03,665 --> 00:02:04,958
Hello, Dr. York?

48
00:02:05,583 --> 00:02:07,919
Emilia, it's good to finally talk to you.

49
00:02:08,002 --> 00:02:10,505
Dr. York, how's my dad doing?

50
00:02:10,588 --> 00:02:11,506
<i>He's okay.</i>

51
00:02:11,589 --> 00:02:13,341
Better than okay, actually.

52
00:02:13,925 --> 00:02:15,885
He's recovering faster than expected.

53
00:02:16,636 --> 00:02:18,263
Um… That's good to know.

54
00:02:18,346 --> 00:02:19,973
Does this mean…

55
00:02:20,056 --> 00:02:21,057
<i>Yes.</i>

56
00:02:21,141 --> 00:02:22,725
He'll be coming home soon.

57
00:02:23,852 --> 00:02:26,604
His right index finger
moved earlier today.

58
00:02:27,438 --> 00:02:28,982
That's wonderful, Doc.

59
00:02:29,065 --> 00:02:30,900
I can't wait for him to come home.

60
00:02:31,484 --> 00:02:32,443
<i>He will.</i>

61
00:02:32,527 --> 00:02:34,946
And possibly, without any complications.

62
00:02:35,697 --> 00:02:37,490
He can continue to serve the people.

63
00:02:38,908 --> 00:02:39,909
Thank you, Doc.

64
00:02:39,993 --> 00:02:42,287
Thank you so much
for taking care of my dad.

65
00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:43,997
All right. I think that will be it.

66
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,623
<i>Thank you very much, Emilia.</i>

67
00:02:45,707 --> 00:02:50,712
[tense music playing]

68
00:02:50,795 --> 00:02:52,714
He can't come back yet.

69
00:02:58,428 --> 00:02:59,220
<i>You.</i>

70
00:02:59,304 --> 00:03:03,016
<i>You and your weaknesses as a woman!</i>

71
00:03:03,099 --> 00:03:04,601
<i>-You never think, do you?</i>
<i>-Ouch!</i>

72
00:03:04,684 --> 00:03:06,227
<i>-Show some dignity!</i>
<i>-Ow!</i>

73
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:07,854
<i>Ouch!</i>

74
00:03:08,396 --> 00:03:10,732
<i>Emilia, you disappoint me.</i>

75
00:03:13,735 --> 00:03:15,528
I don't want to be his slave.

76
00:03:18,656 --> 00:03:20,950
I don't want to be his puppet again.

77
00:03:24,662 --> 00:03:26,748
I understand you, Emilia.

78
00:03:27,665 --> 00:03:29,167
I don't want you

79
00:03:29,250 --> 00:03:33,421
to go through the same thing
my sister did with Julio.

80
00:03:35,882 --> 00:03:39,427
Auntie, I promised Mama
I wouldn't be like her.

81
00:03:45,183 --> 00:03:46,267
[Julio] <i>What?!</i>

82
00:03:47,852 --> 00:03:49,103
<i>You're a disgrace!</i>

83
00:03:49,187 --> 00:03:51,648
<i>You can't even hold a simple event?!</i>

84
00:03:53,274 --> 00:03:55,401
<i>Forgive me, Love. </i>[sobs]

85
00:03:55,485 --> 00:03:56,402
<i>What?!</i>

86
00:03:56,486 --> 00:03:57,528
-<i>"Love"?!</i>
-[crying]

87
00:03:57,612 --> 00:03:58,780
<i>"Mayor"!</i>

88
00:03:58,863 --> 00:04:01,616
<i>Call me "Mayor"! Remember that!</i>

89
00:04:01,699 --> 00:04:03,618
<i>Please forgive me, Mayor.</i>

90
00:04:04,077 --> 00:04:07,080
<i>You couldn't even give me a son,</i>

91
00:04:07,163 --> 00:04:09,707
<i>now you can't even do something</i>
<i>as simple as this for me?!</i>

92
00:04:09,791 --> 00:04:11,793
<i>It won't happen again!</i>

93
00:04:11,876 --> 00:04:13,544
-[sobbing]
-<i>You…</i>

94
00:04:13,628 --> 00:04:15,338
<i>This better not happen again.</i>

95
00:04:15,421 --> 00:04:18,299
<i>Or else you'll suffer worse than this!</i>

96
00:04:20,551 --> 00:04:25,598
[tense music playing]

97
00:04:29,143 --> 00:04:30,436
<i>Ma!</i>

98
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:31,771
-<i>Ma…</i>
-[crying]

99
00:04:31,854 --> 00:04:33,189
<i>Ma, are you all right?!</i>

100
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:39,279
<i>How dare you?!</i>

101
00:04:39,362 --> 00:04:41,281
<i>You keep on giving me nothing but…</i>

102
00:04:41,364 --> 00:04:43,199
-<i>shame and disappointment!</i>
-[sobbing]

103
00:04:43,741 --> 00:04:45,285
<i>You shameful woman!</i>

104
00:04:45,368 --> 00:04:47,829
<i>Your mistress got what she deserved!</i>

105
00:04:47,912 --> 00:04:49,747
<i>Whatever relationship</i>
<i>I have with that woman</i>

106
00:04:49,831 --> 00:04:51,040
<i>is none of your business!</i>

107
00:04:51,124 --> 00:04:52,959
<i>I am your wife!</i>

108
00:04:53,042 --> 00:04:56,087
<i>You are just my wife.</i>

109
00:04:57,046 --> 00:04:59,549
<i>It's your fault why I look</i>
<i>for other women!</i>

110
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:02,010
<i>Just look at yourself!</i>

111
00:05:02,093 --> 00:05:05,305
<i>Who in their right mind would</i>
<i>ever want to sleep with you?!</i>

112
00:05:05,388 --> 00:05:07,348
<i>I became this way because of you!</i>

113
00:05:07,432 --> 00:05:08,891
<i>Oh, so you're blaming me now?</i>

114
00:05:08,975 --> 00:05:10,351
<i>-Stop!</i>
<i>-How dare you?!</i>

115
00:05:10,435 --> 00:05:11,894
<i>That's enough, Papa!</i>

116
00:05:11,978 --> 00:05:13,896
<i>Stay out of this!</i>

117
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:15,231
<i>-You bitch!</i>
<i>-Ah!</i>

118
00:05:15,315 --> 00:05:17,233
<i>What? Are you fighting back now?!</i>

119
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:18,985
-[vase shattering]
-<i>Ah!</i>

120
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:21,863
<i>You little brat.</i>

121
00:05:22,947 --> 00:05:24,866
<i>Are you going against me?!</i>

122
00:05:24,949 --> 00:05:27,160
<i>-No, don't!</i>
<i>-Come here! Come here!</i>

123
00:05:27,243 --> 00:05:28,619
<i>Stop it, Julio!</i>

124
00:05:28,703 --> 00:05:30,663
<i>Hurt me, instead! Not our daughter!</i>

125
00:05:30,747 --> 00:05:31,664
<i>Pa!</i>

126
00:05:31,748 --> 00:05:32,999
<i>Stop it!</i>

127
00:05:33,082 --> 00:05:34,834
[whimpers]

128
00:05:34,917 --> 00:05:36,252
<i>You two can go to hell!</i>

129
00:05:37,045 --> 00:05:38,337
<i>Forgive me, Julio!</i>

130
00:05:38,421 --> 00:05:41,257
<i>Please forgive us! Forgive me!</i>

131
00:05:41,841 --> 00:05:43,468
[sobbing]

132
00:05:43,551 --> 00:05:44,761
<i>Why, Mama?</i>

133
00:05:46,888 --> 00:05:49,348
<i>Why do you let Papa hurt you?</i>

134
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:52,226
<i>Because I'm just a woman, Emilia.</i>

135
00:05:53,811 --> 00:05:55,313
<i>I'm weak.</i>

136
00:05:55,396 --> 00:05:59,275
[crying]

137
00:05:59,358 --> 00:06:00,693
<i>That's not true, Ma.</i>

138
00:06:00,777 --> 00:06:03,613
[crying]

139
00:06:17,794 --> 00:06:24,467
[somber music playing]

140
00:06:29,972 --> 00:06:31,933
My time has come, Aunt Claire.

141
00:06:33,768 --> 00:06:35,019
Papa is gone.

142
00:06:36,104 --> 00:06:37,438
He's over.

143
00:06:37,522 --> 00:06:41,984
[ominous music playing]

144
00:06:42,068 --> 00:06:44,612
I am Emilia Ardiente.

145
00:06:47,949 --> 00:06:51,911
I will be the most
powerful woman in this town…

146
00:06:53,037 --> 00:06:54,872
and the entire country.

147
00:06:54,956 --> 00:06:58,501
[ominous music playing]

148
00:07:23,943 --> 00:07:29,323
[soft music playing]

149
00:07:30,825 --> 00:07:32,368
<i>It was just a kiss.</i>

150
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:34,370
<i>It's no big deal.</i>

151
00:07:34,454 --> 00:07:35,455
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

152
00:07:35,538 --> 00:07:37,457
<i>I know what I did was wrong.</i>

153
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:39,167
<i>But I hope you'll forgive me.</i>

154
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:41,002
<i>Yes, I forgive you.</i>

155
00:07:43,629 --> 00:07:50,636
[soft music playing]

156
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:55,641
Good, you're still up.

157
00:07:56,851 --> 00:07:58,186
I wanted to talk to you.

158
00:07:58,895 --> 00:08:00,104
About what?

159
00:08:01,147 --> 00:08:02,398
About Diego.

160
00:08:05,443 --> 00:08:06,819
Forget it.

161
00:08:06,903 --> 00:08:09,280
He already apologized. We're fine now.

162
00:08:10,156 --> 00:08:11,574
Wait, what?

163
00:08:11,657 --> 00:08:13,951
You're not mad he kissed you?

164
00:08:14,035 --> 00:08:15,953
Ivy, he disrespected you!

165
00:08:16,662 --> 00:08:17,788
Calm down.

166
00:08:18,331 --> 00:08:20,958
He already said sorry. We're fine now.

167
00:08:21,042 --> 00:08:23,669
Besides, I hit him right after,

168
00:08:23,753 --> 00:08:25,338
if that's what you want to hear.

169
00:08:25,421 --> 00:08:27,507
That's not enough.
I could beat him to a pulp.

170
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:29,091
I can break a few bones if you want.

171
00:08:29,175 --> 00:08:30,343
Hang on.

172
00:08:30,551 --> 00:08:31,969
Why are you acting like this?

173
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:35,890
I said we're fine.

174
00:08:38,935 --> 00:08:39,894
Ivy…

175
00:08:39,977 --> 00:08:42,146
I just want to protect
you from the Ardientes.

176
00:08:42,688 --> 00:08:43,940
Especially from those brothers.

177
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:47,318
Besides…

178
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:49,487
I promised Ms. Prianka.

179
00:08:51,781 --> 00:08:52,782
I know.

180
00:08:56,410 --> 00:08:57,662
I know that.

181
00:08:58,037 --> 00:08:59,539
It won't happen again.

182
00:09:01,916 --> 00:09:04,001
I'll keep my distance from Arnaldo.

183
00:09:05,795 --> 00:09:06,796
And Diego, too.

184
00:09:07,838 --> 00:09:08,756
You better.

185
00:09:09,674 --> 00:09:10,675
What?

186
00:09:11,759 --> 00:09:13,678
I said, what's your next move?

187
00:09:19,392 --> 00:09:20,518
[Pablo] Yes.

188
00:09:21,060 --> 00:09:23,479
I will make sure it's legislated.

189
00:09:24,939 --> 00:09:25,940
No!

190
00:09:26,941 --> 00:09:28,150
I don't agree.

191
00:09:28,609 --> 00:09:32,613
Listen, let's just meet
when I return to Manila.

192
00:09:33,364 --> 00:09:35,199
Okay? Bye.

193
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:36,951
[Emilia] Senator.

194
00:09:37,910 --> 00:09:38,869
Emilia.

195
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:42,164
You know, being a senator
must be so hectic.

196
00:09:42,248 --> 00:09:44,292
-All the phone calls, travels…
-[Pablo chuckles]

197
00:09:44,375 --> 00:09:45,626
It looks exhausting.

198
00:09:45,710 --> 00:09:47,420
Not for the weak.

199
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:51,007
I know. Too bad Papa
has to give up his dreams.

200
00:09:52,675 --> 00:09:53,759
What do you mean?

201
00:09:54,677 --> 00:09:56,887
I spoke to his doctor last night.

202
00:09:56,971 --> 00:09:59,432
The prognosis of his recovery
doesn't look too good.

203
00:10:00,224 --> 00:10:01,225
[Pablo sighs]

204
00:10:01,851 --> 00:10:03,561
Too bad for Julio then.

205
00:10:03,769 --> 00:10:04,979
I know, Senator.

206
00:10:05,062 --> 00:10:07,523
That's why I'm formally
withdrawing his candidacy

207
00:10:07,607 --> 00:10:08,899
for this election.

208
00:10:08,983 --> 00:10:11,152
I have to forward this to the party.

209
00:10:11,694 --> 00:10:14,989
We'll find a suitable
replacement for him right away.

210
00:10:15,072 --> 00:10:16,407
Come on, Senator.

211
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:18,242
I repeatedly expressed my interest

212
00:10:18,326 --> 00:10:20,119
in running this election.

213
00:10:20,202 --> 00:10:21,954
Won't you support me?

214
00:10:22,204 --> 00:10:23,623
[Pablo chuckles]

215
00:10:24,206 --> 00:10:26,459
I'm not the only one who decides.

216
00:10:27,501 --> 00:10:29,086
How about this, Senator?

217
00:10:29,170 --> 00:10:32,590
What does the party need
for them to support me?

218
00:10:33,924 --> 00:10:36,761
You know very well
the answer to that, Emilia.

219
00:10:36,844 --> 00:10:37,887
Money?

220
00:10:38,596 --> 00:10:40,640
[chuckles]

221
00:10:40,723 --> 00:10:42,224
Lots of it.

222
00:10:44,101 --> 00:10:45,227
Hmm.

223
00:10:47,021 --> 00:10:50,066
Tell the Land Acquisition Team
to come to Poblacion Ardiente.

224
00:10:50,149 --> 00:10:53,277
I have something I need
to discuss with them.

225
00:10:54,028 --> 00:10:55,071
And…

226
00:10:55,988 --> 00:10:57,031
This one.

227
00:10:58,115 --> 00:11:00,034
Please return it to the Habitat Group.

228
00:11:00,117 --> 00:11:02,953
Tell them it's overpriced.
They should fix it.

229
00:11:03,037 --> 00:11:04,330
Yes, Miss Aguas.

230
00:11:04,580 --> 00:11:07,833
By the way, Governor
Emilia's EA called earlier.

231
00:11:07,958 --> 00:11:09,710
She said she's going to visit.

232
00:11:10,086 --> 00:11:11,170
Okay.

233
00:11:11,253 --> 00:11:12,588
Ivy!

234
00:11:13,297 --> 00:11:14,298
Hi!

235
00:11:15,966 --> 00:11:17,176
-Emilia!
-[Emilia chuckles]

236
00:11:17,259 --> 00:11:18,552
It's nice to see you.

237
00:11:18,636 --> 00:11:20,137
It's nice to see you.

238
00:11:20,805 --> 00:11:22,098
You got here just in time.

239
00:11:22,181 --> 00:11:25,559
I'm arranging EPZ's transfer
to its new site.

240
00:11:25,935 --> 00:11:27,937
Ivy, the EPZ can wait,

241
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:30,022
but what I have to say can't.

242
00:11:31,148 --> 00:11:33,818
I'm going to replace Dad
and run for Senate!

243
00:11:34,443 --> 00:11:37,196
Yes, Ivy! I'm going to be a senator soon!

244
00:11:37,279 --> 00:11:38,406
And when that happens,

245
00:11:38,489 --> 00:11:40,491
we're both going to be unstoppable!

246
00:11:42,785 --> 00:11:43,869
[chuckles]

247
00:11:43,953 --> 00:11:44,995
Congrats! Con…

248
00:11:45,079 --> 00:11:46,705
Congratulations, Emilia.

249
00:11:46,956 --> 00:11:47,915
Uh…

250
00:11:48,207 --> 00:11:49,625
I'm sorry, but…

251
00:11:50,167 --> 00:11:51,127
What about Arnaldo?

252
00:11:51,210 --> 00:11:54,046
I thought he's the one being
groomed by the congressman?

253
00:11:54,463 --> 00:11:56,257
Ivy, Papa's not here,

254
00:11:56,340 --> 00:11:59,218
so I'm the one who calls the shots.

255
00:11:59,844 --> 00:12:02,471
What if Arnaldo protests?

256
00:12:02,555 --> 00:12:03,597
You know how he is.

257
00:12:03,681 --> 00:12:06,100
He's just like his grandfather.

258
00:12:06,642 --> 00:12:08,978
Then, I will do what I do best.

259
00:12:10,938 --> 00:12:14,233
Whoever goes against Governor Emilia…

260
00:12:14,316 --> 00:12:16,777
Oh, come now, Ivy.

261
00:12:16,861 --> 00:12:19,947
You make it sound like I'm very dangerous.

262
00:12:20,156 --> 00:12:21,365
I'm still a mother.

263
00:12:21,449 --> 00:12:23,534
I can always discipline Arnaldo.

264
00:12:26,162 --> 00:12:28,205
What? Aren't you gonna offer me anything?

265
00:12:28,289 --> 00:12:30,416
We should celebrate!

266
00:12:30,666 --> 00:12:32,209
Oh, you're right. Okay.

267
00:12:32,293 --> 00:12:33,627
-Hold on.
-Thank you.

268
00:12:34,503 --> 00:12:38,174
Nanny Carlotta, please get the champagne.

269
00:12:42,052 --> 00:12:43,471
-Let's celebrate.
-I know!

270
00:12:43,554 --> 00:12:44,597
-Can I sit down?
-Yes.

271
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:45,473
Oh, thank you.

272
00:12:45,556 --> 00:12:46,682
Of course, you can sit down…

273
00:12:46,765 --> 00:12:48,809
-<i>Senator </i>Emilia.
-[Emilia chuckles]

274
00:12:50,019 --> 00:12:51,437
This is it!

275
00:12:52,646 --> 00:12:53,647
Nanny!

276
00:12:57,693 --> 00:12:59,153
Shoo the flies away.

277
00:12:59,862 --> 00:13:00,946
Oh, no!

278
00:13:01,655 --> 00:13:02,990
[Claire] The eggs are overcooked.

279
00:13:03,699 --> 00:13:04,783
Cook a new batch.

280
00:13:05,201 --> 00:13:06,744
Take this with you.

281
00:13:06,827 --> 00:13:08,412
Take it back to the kitchen.

282
00:13:12,374 --> 00:13:13,834
[cutlery clanking]

283
00:13:15,002 --> 00:13:16,170
Mamita.

284
00:13:17,922 --> 00:13:19,173
Good morning, Arnaldo.

285
00:13:20,007 --> 00:13:21,175
Good morning.

286
00:13:22,593 --> 00:13:24,970
Sorry, we didn't see
each other last night.

287
00:13:25,679 --> 00:13:26,639
I was tired.

288
00:13:27,264 --> 00:13:28,849
It was such a long flight.

289
00:13:29,725 --> 00:13:31,435
It's okay. Uh…

290
00:13:31,769 --> 00:13:32,978
How are you?

291
00:13:34,188 --> 00:13:35,481
I'm fine.

292
00:13:35,856 --> 00:13:37,024
Still beautiful, I suppose.

293
00:13:37,107 --> 00:13:38,484
I can see that.

294
00:13:39,902 --> 00:13:40,986
By the way…

295
00:13:41,654 --> 00:13:43,656
Your mom told me about you and Diego.

296
00:13:45,950 --> 00:13:47,159
Arnaldo…

297
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:49,453
I want you to patch things up with Diego.

298
00:13:50,412 --> 00:13:54,458
You know how high your mother's
political dreams are.

299
00:13:54,708 --> 00:13:57,419
And your sibling rivalry
will not help her one bit.

300
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:00,464
Mamita, save it.

301
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:03,384
Diego's the one who should
apologize 'cause I'm the mayor.

302
00:14:04,468 --> 00:14:07,137
He should follow and
respect everything I want.

303
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:11,976
But let's not talk about him.

304
00:14:12,059 --> 00:14:13,352
Let's talk about you.

305
00:14:13,435 --> 00:14:14,562
I haven't seen you in so long.

306
00:14:16,605 --> 00:14:18,023
Well, let's eat.

307
00:14:18,941 --> 00:14:24,154
[unsettling music playing]

308
00:14:36,417 --> 00:14:41,672
[unsettling music playing]

309
00:14:43,549 --> 00:14:45,092
What do you want me to do with him?

310
00:14:45,718 --> 00:14:47,261
Just keep his therapy going.

311
00:14:48,512 --> 00:14:49,972
Doc, once he gets better…

312
00:14:51,932 --> 00:14:53,225
Please bring him to this address.

313
00:14:55,978 --> 00:14:57,146
I'll handle it.

314
00:14:57,938 --> 00:15:01,692
[suspenseful music playing]

315
00:15:09,033 --> 00:15:10,117
[Loring] There. Okay.

316
00:15:11,035 --> 00:15:12,369
-Put it down there.
-[Diego grunts]

317
00:15:12,453 --> 00:15:13,245
Hold on, Nanny.

318
00:15:13,329 --> 00:15:14,622
Why? What's wrong?

319
00:15:14,705 --> 00:15:15,664
I need a break.

320
00:15:15,748 --> 00:15:17,458
-[Diego huffs]
-Are you tired?

321
00:15:17,541 --> 00:15:18,709
Water, Nanny?

322
00:15:19,209 --> 00:15:20,961
Drink up, boy.

323
00:15:21,545 --> 00:15:22,588
I'm fine.

324
00:15:24,632 --> 00:15:25,591
Loring?

325
00:15:25,674 --> 00:15:26,425
-Loring.
-Yes?

326
00:15:26,508 --> 00:15:27,384
Mr. Dolfo?

327
00:15:27,468 --> 00:15:29,178
-What brings you here?
-Diego!

328
00:15:31,388 --> 00:15:33,766
I wanted to ask a favor.

329
00:15:34,308 --> 00:15:35,351
What is it?

330
00:15:35,434 --> 00:15:38,771
Can you help me bring these

331
00:15:38,854 --> 00:15:40,397
to Miss Ivy's house?

332
00:15:40,898 --> 00:15:42,691
I just want to thank her.

333
00:15:44,109 --> 00:15:45,903
Sure thing. No problem.

334
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:47,655
Thank you very much.

335
00:15:48,113 --> 00:15:49,448
Diego! Diego!

336
00:15:49,531 --> 00:15:50,950
-Hey, Butchoy!
-Butchoy!

337
00:15:52,242 --> 00:15:54,286
I want to come, too.

338
00:15:54,370 --> 00:15:56,538
I want to give this to Miss Beautiful.

339
00:15:56,622 --> 00:15:58,415
It's her favorite.

340
00:15:58,499 --> 00:16:00,000
[Loring and Dolfo coo]

341
00:16:00,084 --> 00:16:01,335
[Loring chuckles]

342
00:16:01,418 --> 00:16:02,920
All right. I'll give it to her.

343
00:16:03,003 --> 00:16:04,672
Diego. come closer.

344
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:06,632
-He has more.
-What?

345
00:16:06,715 --> 00:16:09,343
I have a letter for her.

346
00:16:12,429 --> 00:16:13,764
Wow!

347
00:16:13,847 --> 00:16:17,393
Hey, aren't you a little
too young for love letters?

348
00:16:17,476 --> 00:16:19,144
You're something else, huh?

349
00:16:19,228 --> 00:16:22,147
Someone might beat me to her.

350
00:16:23,023 --> 00:16:24,566
[Loring] That's right.

351
00:16:24,650 --> 00:16:27,528
[imitating Butchoy]
Someone here just might.

352
00:16:28,237 --> 00:16:29,363
Right?

353
00:16:29,488 --> 00:16:30,948
[cooing]

354
00:16:39,331 --> 00:16:40,624
Arnaldo, join us.

355
00:16:41,375 --> 00:16:42,376
Good evening.

356
00:16:44,586 --> 00:16:46,880
Are we celebrating something, Mom?

357
00:16:47,423 --> 00:16:49,091
I'm glad you mentioned it.

358
00:16:49,174 --> 00:16:50,843
As a matter of fact, we are.

359
00:16:51,969 --> 00:16:54,013
Senator Pablo spoke to me.

360
00:16:54,096 --> 00:16:56,140
And it's final, I'm running for Senate.

361
00:16:56,223 --> 00:16:58,934
[tense music playing]

362
00:17:00,102 --> 00:17:01,103
But, Mom…

363
00:17:01,395 --> 00:17:03,689
Arnaldo, it's final.

364
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:06,358
Senator Pablo already spoke to me.

365
00:17:06,608 --> 00:17:08,819
You know how hard it is to refuse him.

366
00:17:11,321 --> 00:17:12,489
Arnaldo, look.

367
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:14,033
Now is my time.

368
00:17:14,324 --> 00:17:15,659
And when your time comes,

369
00:17:15,743 --> 00:17:17,369
I'll be your greatest supporter.

370
00:17:17,453 --> 00:17:19,496
But for now, I need your support.

371
00:17:19,580 --> 00:17:22,332
[tense music playing]

372
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:28,255
Excuse me.

373
00:17:28,338 --> 00:17:29,214
Arnaldo?

374
00:17:29,965 --> 00:17:31,091
Arnaldo!

375
00:17:39,933 --> 00:17:40,934
Let's eat.

376
00:17:43,812 --> 00:17:47,399
[tense music playing]

377
00:17:50,235 --> 00:17:51,779
I have to stop Emilia.

378
00:17:51,862 --> 00:17:53,489
I can't let her run for senator.

379
00:17:53,572 --> 00:17:55,324
If she wins,

380
00:17:55,574 --> 00:17:56,742
she'll have the power

381
00:17:56,825 --> 00:17:58,368
to manipulate our judicial system.

382
00:17:58,869 --> 00:18:01,955
It'll be hard to seek justice
if that happens.

383
00:18:02,039 --> 00:18:03,457
What will you do?

384
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:07,961
Ivy.

385
00:18:09,129 --> 00:18:10,130
Jepoy.

386
00:18:10,714 --> 00:18:11,965
Have you found them?

387
00:18:12,716 --> 00:18:14,843
Arthur's already recovering safely.

388
00:18:15,177 --> 00:18:17,179
We have Tonio, too.

389
00:18:17,304 --> 00:18:20,140
<i>-Nice! My cards are great.</i>
<i>-I quit. I have a bad draw.</i>

390
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:22,643
<i>You're such a spoilsport.</i>

391
00:18:22,726 --> 00:18:24,853
<i>-We struck gold again.</i>
<i>-All right!</i>

392
00:18:24,937 --> 00:18:26,980
<i>-That looks good!</i>
<i>-I know!</i>

393
00:18:27,064 --> 00:18:28,315
<i>That's not even enough for Mario.</i>

394
00:18:28,398 --> 00:18:29,191
[laughs]

395
00:18:29,274 --> 00:18:31,610
<i>That's why we should just behave,</i>

396
00:18:31,693 --> 00:18:33,612
<i>and the Ardientes will</i>
<i>take care of us, right?</i>

397
00:18:33,695 --> 00:18:34,446
<i>-Yeah.</i>
<i>-Right.</i>

398
00:18:34,530 --> 00:18:36,990
[goon 1] <i>I don't wanna end up like Tonio.</i>

399
00:18:37,991 --> 00:18:38,992
<i>Who's Tonio?</i>

400
00:18:39,284 --> 00:18:41,286
<i>Oh, right, he doesn't know him.</i>

401
00:18:41,453 --> 00:18:43,539
<i>He was the governor's number one hit man.</i>

402
00:18:43,622 --> 00:18:45,541
<i>He was still the mayor then, right?</i>

403
00:18:45,958 --> 00:18:47,126
<i>Have you heard anything about him?</i>

404
00:18:47,209 --> 00:18:48,752
[goon 2] <i>The governor</i>
<i>probably had killed him.</i>

405
00:18:48,836 --> 00:18:50,629
<i>He knew too much.</i>

406
00:18:51,547 --> 00:18:52,422
[Ivy] Good.

407
00:18:54,133 --> 00:18:55,843
But we need more evidence.

408
00:18:55,926 --> 00:18:58,178
I do have some evidence,
but it's not enough.

409
00:18:58,262 --> 00:19:00,889
I have Emilia on record admitting

410
00:19:00,973 --> 00:19:02,766
her family runs the town's
illegal gambling dens.

411
00:19:03,934 --> 00:19:07,938
But I need more whistleblowers
against Emilia.

412
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:10,399
And we will use that evidence

413
00:19:10,482 --> 00:19:12,609
to strengthen our testimony

414
00:19:12,693 --> 00:19:15,112
and take down the Ardientes.

415
00:19:21,660 --> 00:19:23,996
Since Arthur is recovering,

416
00:19:24,079 --> 00:19:26,248
he's still no good to us.

417
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:28,792
What about Tonio?

418
00:19:30,377 --> 00:19:31,879
You know what to do.

419
00:19:32,754 --> 00:19:33,797
But Ivy…

420
00:19:33,881 --> 00:19:35,591
What is it this time?

421
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:37,885
There you go again, Jepoy!

422
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:39,761
Thank you for your concern.

423
00:19:40,012 --> 00:19:42,055
You just want to protect me.
I know that already!

424
00:19:42,973 --> 00:19:44,933
But I need you to do this.

425
00:19:45,017 --> 00:19:46,518
You're the only one I can trust

426
00:19:46,602 --> 00:19:47,853
when it comes to Tonio.

427
00:19:48,103 --> 00:19:50,397
So, please, set those
concerns aside for now.

428
00:19:51,648 --> 00:19:52,566
Go on.

429
00:19:52,649 --> 00:19:54,860
If you have to,
ask for a leave from Arnaldo,

430
00:19:54,943 --> 00:19:57,321
so you can focus on your task.

431
00:20:00,115 --> 00:20:02,326
Jepoy, don't give me that look.

432
00:20:02,993 --> 00:20:04,203
Go!

433
00:20:04,703 --> 00:20:05,704
All right.

434
00:20:06,830 --> 00:20:08,248
I still have a lot of work to do.

435
00:20:08,916 --> 00:20:11,668
[unsettling music playing]

436
00:20:11,877 --> 00:20:13,086
[phone ringing]

437
00:20:15,255 --> 00:20:16,757
-[sighs]
-[phone ringing]

438
00:20:17,591 --> 00:20:18,634
Senator?

439
00:20:20,844 --> 00:20:22,554
Good evening, Miss Aguas.

440
00:20:22,638 --> 00:20:25,349
I'd like to invite you out
for dinner, Miss Aguas.

441
00:20:25,974 --> 00:20:26,975
<i>Are you free?</i>

442
00:20:27,267 --> 00:20:30,729
It depends on what the dinner is for.

443
00:20:33,732 --> 00:20:36,068
I'm sure Emilia already approached you…

444
00:20:36,526 --> 00:20:39,321
<i>…regarding her senatorial ambition.</i>

445
00:20:40,364 --> 00:20:41,573
Let me guess.

446
00:20:41,949 --> 00:20:46,536
Emilia spoke to you
to convince me to support her.

447
00:20:47,287 --> 00:20:48,538
No, Miss Aguas.

448
00:20:49,456 --> 00:20:50,749
<i>On the contrary…</i>

449
00:20:51,458 --> 00:20:53,794
I have a different candidate in mind.

450
00:20:55,254 --> 00:20:57,089
I want you to support them.

451
00:20:58,757 --> 00:21:00,425
A different candidate?

452
00:21:01,176 --> 00:21:02,386
I like the sound of that.

453
00:21:03,053 --> 00:21:04,096
<i>Okay, Senator.</i>

454
00:21:04,179 --> 00:21:06,515
Text me which restaurant.

455
00:21:06,598 --> 00:21:08,058
I'll be there.

456
00:21:13,689 --> 00:21:15,440
Nanny, I won't be having dinner here.

457
00:21:15,524 --> 00:21:17,317
I need to meet with the senator.

458
00:21:17,401 --> 00:21:19,736
I think he's going along with my plan.

459
00:21:20,570 --> 00:21:21,571
All right, dear.

460
00:21:22,155 --> 00:21:23,407
I'll go get changed.

461
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:29,288
Please take care.

462
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:34,960
[unsettling music playing]

463
00:21:36,211 --> 00:21:37,254
Grandpa?

464
00:21:37,879 --> 00:21:39,172
Can you hear me?

465
00:21:39,423 --> 00:21:41,425
<i>It's Arnaldo, your favorite grandson.</i>

466
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:44,886
Please wake up, Grandpa.

467
00:21:45,345 --> 00:21:46,763
I need you here.

468
00:21:51,643 --> 00:21:54,855
Mom's getting out of control.

469
00:21:54,938 --> 00:21:56,440
I don't know what to do anymore.

470
00:21:57,733 --> 00:21:59,943
[Julio] <i>I had this made for you, Arnaldo.</i>

471
00:22:00,027 --> 00:22:02,321
<i>You have to study this,</i>

472
00:22:02,404 --> 00:22:05,991
<i>till you can control every piece of it</i>

473
00:22:06,074 --> 00:22:07,617
<i>from wherever you are.</i>

474
00:22:07,909 --> 00:22:11,955
<i>That is the mark of a true leader.</i>

475
00:22:13,957 --> 00:22:18,170
<i>When I'm gone, all this will be yours.</i>

476
00:22:18,253 --> 00:22:22,758
<i>You will be the king</i>
<i>of Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

477
00:22:23,008 --> 00:22:25,761
<i>Take good care of our name.</i>

478
00:22:27,846 --> 00:22:29,806
I promise, Grandpa.

479
00:22:31,683 --> 00:22:32,976
[sighs]

480
00:22:33,060 --> 00:22:34,352
I won't fail you.

481
00:22:35,771 --> 00:22:38,065
I will protect the interest of our name,

482
00:22:38,148 --> 00:22:39,357
no matter what.

483
00:22:42,527 --> 00:22:43,528
[exhales sharply]

484
00:22:55,707 --> 00:23:02,214
[ominous music playing]

485
00:23:04,716 --> 00:23:09,679
[heart monitor beeping]

486
00:23:12,140 --> 00:23:16,228
[bright music playing]

487
00:23:16,978 --> 00:23:20,315
[Loring and Pandoy snickering]

488
00:23:20,398 --> 00:23:24,402
Looks like you're off to court someone.

489
00:23:24,486 --> 00:23:26,488
-Court someone?
-Hmm?

490
00:23:26,571 --> 00:23:27,823
I'm just going to deliver

491
00:23:27,906 --> 00:23:30,659
Mr. Dolfo and Butchoy's gifts to Ivy.

492
00:23:30,742 --> 00:23:32,828
Well, at least Butchoy isn't afraid…

493
00:23:32,911 --> 00:23:34,663
-to show his feelings.
-That's right.

494
00:23:34,746 --> 00:23:35,831
Exactly.

495
00:23:35,914 --> 00:23:37,249
I'm not afraid, okay?

496
00:23:37,332 --> 00:23:38,083
[both] Oh?

497
00:23:38,166 --> 00:23:39,876
Then prove it.

498
00:23:40,335 --> 00:23:41,419
[Loring and Pandoy giggling]

499
00:23:41,503 --> 00:23:43,755
You'd like that, huh?

500
00:23:43,922 --> 00:23:46,299
But how can he prove it?

501
00:23:46,383 --> 00:23:49,136
He's not going there to court her.

502
00:23:49,219 --> 00:23:52,055
He's just dropping off
a letter and some flowers

503
00:23:52,139 --> 00:23:53,140
from Butchoy.

504
00:23:53,223 --> 00:23:55,392
Because Butchoy isn't shy!

505
00:23:55,475 --> 00:23:57,144
-He's serious about her!
-You're so silly!

506
00:23:57,227 --> 00:23:59,020
[Pandoy] Then why dress up
just to deliver flowers?

507
00:23:59,104 --> 00:24:01,231
-He's looking sharp.
-Oh, stop it, will you?

508
00:24:01,314 --> 00:24:02,816
Hey! Why are you blushing?

509
00:24:02,899 --> 00:24:03,650
What?!

510
00:24:03,733 --> 00:24:06,153
-No, I'm not!
-[laughter]

511
00:24:06,236 --> 00:24:09,114
[giggling]

512
00:24:09,197 --> 00:24:12,409
[laughing and cooing]

513
00:24:12,492 --> 00:24:14,035
-[Diego] I have to go.
-He's excited!

514
00:24:14,119 --> 00:24:15,954
We're just admiring how handsome you are.

515
00:24:16,037 --> 00:24:17,122
This is special.

516
00:24:17,455 --> 00:24:19,249
-Hmm?
-Ooh?

517
00:24:19,332 --> 00:24:20,959
Quit it, you two.

518
00:24:23,086 --> 00:24:24,379
I'll just text you, Nanny.

519
00:24:24,462 --> 00:24:26,173
Okay. Please take care.

520
00:24:26,256 --> 00:24:27,257
I will.

521
00:24:28,758 --> 00:24:30,969
Butchoy, Mr. Dolfo, ma'am…

522
00:24:31,052 --> 00:24:32,179
Diego…

523
00:24:32,262 --> 00:24:33,930
What are you doing here?

524
00:24:34,097 --> 00:24:37,309
Ivy, they said they wanted
to give you something.

525
00:24:39,186 --> 00:24:40,604
For you, Miss Ivy.

526
00:24:42,105 --> 00:24:43,398
[Dolfo] Thank you very much.

527
00:24:43,857 --> 00:24:46,610
I'm really sorry for what I did, ma'am.

528
00:24:47,277 --> 00:24:50,071
Mr. Dolfo, we already talked about this.

529
00:24:50,155 --> 00:24:52,115
I understand how you felt.

530
00:24:52,199 --> 00:24:53,408
But thank you.

531
00:24:53,491 --> 00:24:55,243
-You're welcome.
-Just put it down here.

532
00:24:57,120 --> 00:24:58,288
And you?

533
00:24:58,914 --> 00:25:00,582
Why are you here?

534
00:25:00,832 --> 00:25:02,709
For you, Miss Beautiful.

535
00:25:03,501 --> 00:25:04,920
[chuckles]

536
00:25:05,462 --> 00:25:06,588
You're so cute!

537
00:25:06,671 --> 00:25:07,839
And you're so sweet, too!

538
00:25:09,466 --> 00:25:10,884
Thank you for these.

539
00:25:10,967 --> 00:25:12,886
Mr. Dolfo, let's go back to the car.

540
00:25:14,638 --> 00:25:15,680
[chuckles softly]

541
00:25:15,764 --> 00:25:17,098
Hey, Butchoy!

542
00:25:17,182 --> 00:25:18,308
Your other gift!

543
00:25:18,934 --> 00:25:20,977
You give it to her, Diego!

544
00:25:23,939 --> 00:25:24,981
Uh…

545
00:25:26,399 --> 00:25:27,609
[chuckles]

546
00:25:28,902 --> 00:25:31,988
Butchoy has a love letter for you.

547
00:25:32,864 --> 00:25:34,741
A love letter? [chuckles]

548
00:25:34,824 --> 00:25:36,326
He's so cute.

549
00:25:38,912 --> 00:25:39,913
I guess…

550
00:25:40,413 --> 00:25:42,290
I've got more competition now.

551
00:25:46,127 --> 00:25:47,087
What?

552
00:25:47,170 --> 00:25:50,423
[soft music playing]

553
00:25:50,590 --> 00:25:52,175
I said, he's too young for that.

554
00:25:56,179 --> 00:25:57,180
[Ivy] Oh.

555
00:25:58,098 --> 00:25:59,224
Ah, yes.

556
00:25:59,557 --> 00:26:02,686
Butchoy is still too young
to think about love.

557
00:26:03,895 --> 00:26:04,938
And…

558
00:26:05,438 --> 00:26:07,816
You know, love is just a distraction.

559
00:26:08,316 --> 00:26:10,151
Especially from important things.

560
00:26:10,944 --> 00:26:13,446
Like Butchoy's studies.

561
00:26:17,117 --> 00:26:20,036
Anyway, Diego, I have to go.
I have an appointment.

562
00:26:20,120 --> 00:26:21,871
Butchoy, Mr. Dolfo, ma'am?

563
00:26:21,955 --> 00:26:23,164
I'll be going now.

564
00:26:23,248 --> 00:26:25,208
-Bye! Take care!
-Take care, Diego.

565
00:26:33,341 --> 00:26:35,218
Thank you for coming, Miss Aguas.

566
00:26:36,052 --> 00:26:38,388
Why am I here again, Senator?

567
00:26:39,347 --> 00:26:40,765
It's about the Ardientes.

568
00:26:41,683 --> 00:26:44,352
I'm worried, especially about Emilia.

569
00:26:45,061 --> 00:26:49,274
She's been making
a fool of herself lately.

570
00:26:49,399 --> 00:26:51,568
Ah. Senator…

571
00:26:52,152 --> 00:26:53,361
Be careful.

572
00:26:53,653 --> 00:26:55,322
I'm Emilia's friend.

573
00:26:56,614 --> 00:26:58,116
I might just tell her what you said.

574
00:26:58,366 --> 00:26:59,826
[chuckles]

575
00:27:01,161 --> 00:27:02,787
You won't do that.

576
00:27:03,621 --> 00:27:06,207
Because you don't play
that way, Miss Aguas.

577
00:27:06,291 --> 00:27:07,500
[chuckles]

578
00:27:09,586 --> 00:27:10,462
So…

579
00:27:11,129 --> 00:27:12,881
Emilia must've approached you

580
00:27:12,964 --> 00:27:15,675
about replacing Julio in the senate race.

581
00:27:15,884 --> 00:27:18,511
And you have a problem with that because?

582
00:27:18,970 --> 00:27:20,221
Because…

583
00:27:21,473 --> 00:27:22,682
She isn't ready.

584
00:27:23,391 --> 00:27:27,687
I'm afraid how it could possibly affect me

585
00:27:27,771 --> 00:27:29,064
and the whole party

586
00:27:29,147 --> 00:27:33,443
if her endorsement pushes through.

587
00:27:33,943 --> 00:27:36,654
Senator, the solution is very simple.

588
00:27:37,113 --> 00:27:38,948
Don't endorse her.

589
00:27:40,200 --> 00:27:41,576
It's not that easy.

590
00:27:41,659 --> 00:27:44,704
And you need me to make it easy? Hmm?

591
00:27:45,705 --> 00:27:47,165
[laughs]

592
00:27:48,583 --> 00:27:50,668
Very smart, Miss Aguas.

593
00:27:50,794 --> 00:27:55,090
What will I gain from this, Senator?

594
00:27:55,173 --> 00:27:56,633
I'll support you…

595
00:27:57,300 --> 00:27:59,969
in your future business endeavors.

596
00:28:01,137 --> 00:28:05,016
I'll even bend some rules
for you, Miss Aguas,

597
00:28:05,266 --> 00:28:06,976
if that's what you need.

598
00:28:07,852 --> 00:28:10,146
Senator, I can handle my own.

599
00:28:11,231 --> 00:28:12,273
But…

600
00:28:12,607 --> 00:28:14,275
If I say yes…

601
00:28:14,818 --> 00:28:16,361
what would I have to do?

602
00:28:16,820 --> 00:28:19,614
What would you like me to do?

603
00:28:22,742 --> 00:28:25,036
I want you to support Arnaldo.

604
00:28:25,120 --> 00:28:28,957
[tense music playing]

605
00:28:39,342 --> 00:28:40,885
You're free for tonight, Madrigal.

606
00:28:41,136 --> 00:28:42,303
Report to me tomorrow.

607
00:28:42,387 --> 00:28:44,180
I'd like to ask
for your permission, Mayor.

608
00:28:44,347 --> 00:28:46,891
I have to go to Manila
for a family emergency.

609
00:28:47,809 --> 00:28:49,269
How long will you be gone?

610
00:28:49,352 --> 00:28:50,729
About two days.

611
00:28:52,313 --> 00:28:54,357
-Sure.
-Thank you, Mayor.

612
00:28:54,983 --> 00:28:57,110
Make sure you're going to your family.

613
00:28:58,486 --> 00:29:01,448
I don't like being betrayed
by the people I trust.

614
00:29:02,198 --> 00:29:05,618
[tense music playing]

615
00:29:11,541 --> 00:29:14,794
[Pablo] <i>A lot of people say</i>
<i>he's too young.</i>

616
00:29:16,004 --> 00:29:17,756
But I believe in him.

617
00:29:18,548 --> 00:29:21,092
Julio trained him, after all.

618
00:29:21,968 --> 00:29:22,969
Wow.

619
00:29:24,512 --> 00:29:26,931
Arnaldo and Emilia…

620
00:29:27,766 --> 00:29:31,102
You want to pit the son
against his mother, Senator?

621
00:29:32,771 --> 00:29:33,980
Exactly.

622
00:29:35,190 --> 00:29:38,026
And competitions like this…

623
00:29:38,818 --> 00:29:41,070
produce good results.

624
00:29:41,321 --> 00:29:43,907
You will benefit
from this, too, Miss Aguas.

625
00:29:48,703 --> 00:29:53,875
As long as I won't get caught in between.

626
00:29:54,542 --> 00:29:56,252
I will make sure of that.

627
00:29:57,962 --> 00:29:59,464
You owe me.

628
00:30:00,965 --> 00:30:02,509
And I am generous…

629
00:30:02,926 --> 00:30:05,887
when it comes to returning
favors, Miss Aguas.

630
00:30:07,347 --> 00:30:08,389
[glasses clink]

631
00:30:11,392 --> 00:30:14,729
Arnaldo versus Emilia.

632
00:30:16,064 --> 00:30:17,398
[chuckles]

633
00:30:23,947 --> 00:30:25,865
Why the long face?

634
00:30:25,949 --> 00:30:27,200
What happened?

635
00:30:27,283 --> 00:30:28,284
Huh?

636
00:30:29,536 --> 00:30:33,665
Well, I just gave Ivy
what I had to give her.

637
00:30:35,041 --> 00:30:40,797
But you couldn't say what you needed to.

638
00:30:41,881 --> 00:30:43,842
-Hmm?
-Exactly, Uncle.

639
00:30:44,425 --> 00:30:47,762
I ended up saying things I shouldn't have.

640
00:30:47,929 --> 00:30:50,306
-Hmm?
-Huh? What do you mean?

641
00:30:50,974 --> 00:30:52,225
[Loring] You mean like…

642
00:30:52,308 --> 00:30:54,185
"I love you, are you okay?"

643
00:30:54,686 --> 00:30:56,855
-Nanny, that's not it.
-[chuckling]

644
00:30:56,938 --> 00:31:01,150
Well, Diego, what exactly
did you want to tell Miss Ivy?

645
00:31:01,234 --> 00:31:04,195
-We are getting really confused.
-Yeah.

646
00:31:04,279 --> 00:31:05,238
[Loring] Okay, look.

647
00:31:05,321 --> 00:31:07,949
First, you were always fighting.

648
00:31:08,199 --> 00:31:10,326
And then you made up

649
00:31:10,410 --> 00:31:12,203
and became friendly.

650
00:31:12,287 --> 00:31:13,913
Then you were fighting again.

651
00:31:14,205 --> 00:31:15,915
But you saved her.

652
00:31:15,999 --> 00:31:18,376
Then you fought again.

653
00:31:18,459 --> 00:31:19,836
And then…

654
00:31:19,919 --> 00:31:23,089
We don't know what happened after.

655
00:31:23,172 --> 00:31:25,800
And now we see you getting all dressed up

656
00:31:25,884 --> 00:31:27,468
just to visit her.

657
00:31:27,552 --> 00:31:31,514
Is there something you're not telling us?

658
00:31:33,016 --> 00:31:33,975
[deep sigh]

659
00:31:34,058 --> 00:31:35,101
-Hmm?
-Oh?

660
00:31:35,184 --> 00:31:37,645
He's blushing. I guess there's something.

661
00:31:37,729 --> 00:31:39,272
-[Pandoy chuckles]
-Uh…

662
00:31:39,355 --> 00:31:42,942
Let's just say I want us
to be friends first

663
00:31:43,026 --> 00:31:46,321
so we could know each other better.

664
00:31:47,155 --> 00:31:48,364
Let's leave it at that.

665
00:31:48,448 --> 00:31:49,741
Ah…

666
00:31:50,450 --> 00:31:52,869
But what if…

667
00:31:53,494 --> 00:31:55,121
What if Lily returns?

668
00:32:01,419 --> 00:32:05,673
[soft music playing]

669
00:32:09,218 --> 00:32:10,428
-Nanny.
-Ivy.

670
00:32:10,720 --> 00:32:11,930
How did it go?

671
00:32:12,931 --> 00:32:15,058
By the way, Joan called.

672
00:32:15,141 --> 00:32:18,603
She'll be here by 9 tomorrow
for your meeting.

673
00:32:18,686 --> 00:32:20,605
Have some tea first.

674
00:32:21,356 --> 00:32:22,398
Thank you.

675
00:32:22,899 --> 00:32:25,944
My dinner with the senator went well.

676
00:32:26,444 --> 00:32:28,947
I got what I needed.

677
00:32:30,573 --> 00:32:32,909
And since Jepoy won't be here tomorrow,

678
00:32:32,992 --> 00:32:36,579
I'll take care of the farmers'
problem with their land.

679
00:32:36,913 --> 00:32:39,958
I'm sure Diego and the farmers
will be glad.

680
00:32:40,959 --> 00:32:44,963
["Sa'Yo" instrumental playing]

681
00:32:46,214 --> 00:32:48,508
I'll just have tea next time.

682
00:32:49,050 --> 00:32:51,260
I'm going to bed.

683
00:32:52,512 --> 00:32:54,347
-Okay, then.
-Good night.

684
00:32:54,889 --> 00:32:56,140
Good night, dear.

685
00:32:57,934 --> 00:33:03,106
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

686
00:33:05,733 --> 00:33:07,944
[Loring] <i>But what if…</i>

687
00:33:08,569 --> 00:33:10,697
<i>What if Lily returns?</i>

688
00:33:42,353 --> 00:33:46,733
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

689
00:33:46,816 --> 00:33:50,028
<i>It's been 13 years since you left.</i>

690
00:33:59,787 --> 00:34:05,668
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

691
00:34:29,525 --> 00:34:34,864
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

692
00:34:38,493 --> 00:34:39,827
[Butchoy] <i>Dear Miss Beautiful,</i>

693
00:34:39,911 --> 00:34:41,913
<i>I just want to thank you</i>

694
00:34:42,205 --> 00:34:44,499
<i>for all the help you've given us.</i>

695
00:34:45,958 --> 00:34:50,963
<i>I also want to thank you</i>
<i>for teaching me to be brave.</i>

696
00:34:51,422 --> 00:34:54,050
<i>And even though I'm weak and fat,</i>

697
00:34:54,342 --> 00:34:56,844
<i>you still think I'm cute.</i>

698
00:34:58,179 --> 00:35:00,890
<i>I promise to exercise more,</i>

699
00:35:00,973 --> 00:35:05,520
<i>so I'll be as fit and handsome as Diego.</i>

700
00:35:07,772 --> 00:35:12,276
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary
continues playing]

701
00:35:15,863 --> 00:35:17,490
<i>It's been 13 years.</i>

702
00:35:19,200 --> 00:35:22,245
<i>We had beautiful memories together.</i>

703
00:35:23,788 --> 00:35:26,290
<i>But I have to forget you, Diego.</i>

704
00:35:32,630 --> 00:35:35,883
I spoke to Daddy earlier, and he told me

705
00:35:35,967 --> 00:35:41,139
that the political party
is considering you…

706
00:35:42,640 --> 00:35:45,977
to run for senator in the next election.

707
00:35:46,227 --> 00:35:47,186
What?

708
00:35:48,229 --> 00:35:49,897
Meaning, I'll be replacing Grandpa?

709
00:35:49,981 --> 00:35:51,023
Well…

710
00:35:51,440 --> 00:35:53,484
If your mom backs out,

711
00:35:53,568 --> 00:35:56,487
or if they don't choose her.

712
00:35:57,029 --> 00:35:57,947
Okay, that's weird.

713
00:35:58,030 --> 00:36:02,118
Mom said the party
already chose to endorse her.

714
00:36:02,326 --> 00:36:03,953
Daddy didn't mention that.

715
00:36:05,246 --> 00:36:08,249
Maybe Aunt Emilia misinterpreted it.

716
00:36:09,792 --> 00:36:10,793
Maybe.

717
00:36:11,919 --> 00:36:13,838
But I'll take this seriously.

718
00:36:14,714 --> 00:36:18,009
I'll make sure the party
is going to endorse me.

719
00:36:18,885 --> 00:36:19,969
[chuckles]

720
00:36:20,052 --> 00:36:23,222
That's my boyfriend.

721
00:36:24,056 --> 00:36:25,975
That's my future senator.

722
00:36:26,142 --> 00:36:28,936
And that's my future husband.

723
00:36:29,395 --> 00:36:30,813
I'm so proud of you.

724
00:36:31,355 --> 00:36:32,356
Thank you.

725
00:36:33,399 --> 00:36:34,901
You're so powerful.

726
00:36:36,485 --> 00:36:41,574
[ominous music playing]

727
00:36:46,204 --> 00:36:47,997
This deed of donation is not valid.

728
00:36:48,080 --> 00:36:50,917
Julio Ardiente's father did not sign it.

729
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:52,418
And since he's long dead…

730
00:36:53,211 --> 00:36:54,378
this is useless.

731
00:36:54,462 --> 00:36:58,507
[tense music playing]

732
00:36:58,591 --> 00:36:59,967
And the congressman…

733
00:37:00,927 --> 00:37:05,223
transferred this property to
Arnaldo Ardiente ten years ago.

734
00:37:05,681 --> 00:37:08,267
That's why he's the key
to legally transferring

735
00:37:08,517 --> 00:37:11,687
the land ownership
directly to the farmers.

736
00:37:11,771 --> 00:37:12,897
Yes, Miss Aguas.

737
00:37:13,189 --> 00:37:15,524
Mr. Torillo can draft a
new deed of donation

738
00:37:15,608 --> 00:37:16,734
for the farmers.

739
00:37:18,361 --> 00:37:19,695
Leave that to me.

740
00:37:20,196 --> 00:37:23,199
Joan, can you attend to my other concerns?

741
00:37:23,574 --> 00:37:25,076
Like the property I want to buy.

742
00:37:25,493 --> 00:37:26,953
It's named under…

743
00:37:28,079 --> 00:37:29,622
Attorney Dante Cruz.

744
00:37:30,081 --> 00:37:32,041
Yes, Miss Aguas. I'm on top of it.

745
00:37:32,792 --> 00:37:34,835
Okay, we're done here. Thank you.

746
00:37:34,919 --> 00:37:36,003
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

747
00:37:36,087 --> 00:37:37,088
Thank you, ma'am.

748
00:37:38,589 --> 00:37:43,761
[tense music playing]

749
00:37:56,023 --> 00:38:00,444
[bright music playing]

750
00:38:10,663 --> 00:38:15,501
[bright music continues playing]

751
00:38:22,383 --> 00:38:24,468
<i>I want to give this to Miss Beautiful.</i>

752
00:38:24,552 --> 00:38:26,304
<i>It's her favorite.</i>

753
00:38:33,477 --> 00:38:35,271
[music fading]

754
00:38:36,605 --> 00:38:37,606
[giggling]

755
00:38:38,566 --> 00:38:39,692
Mr. Mayor.

756
00:38:40,359 --> 00:38:41,402
[Arnaldo] Miss Aguas.

757
00:38:41,610 --> 00:38:42,820
Sorry, um…

758
00:38:42,903 --> 00:38:44,113
What are you doing here?

759
00:38:45,031 --> 00:38:48,451
How dare you show your face
to me after what you did.

760
00:38:48,868 --> 00:38:51,495
Mr. Mayor, I need to consult
something with you.

761
00:38:52,163 --> 00:38:53,164
Aww.

762
00:38:54,165 --> 00:38:55,166
Too bad!

763
00:38:55,249 --> 00:38:56,917
You don't have an appointment.

764
00:38:57,001 --> 00:38:59,003
-Why don't you just leave?
-[Ivy chuckles]

765
00:38:59,587 --> 00:39:01,505
Mr. Mayor, I didn't know you had

766
00:39:01,589 --> 00:39:03,382
a new secretary and…

767
00:39:04,091 --> 00:39:05,468
a new nanny.

768
00:39:05,551 --> 00:39:06,886
-What?!
-Natalie.

769
00:39:06,969 --> 00:39:08,262
Please, please, no.

770
00:39:08,346 --> 00:39:09,805
Don't do that.

771
00:39:09,889 --> 00:39:11,349
It's my fault.

772
00:39:11,432 --> 00:39:14,477
I forgot to put my meeting
with Miss Aguas in my schedule.

773
00:39:14,560 --> 00:39:17,146
So, you can go now. I have to work.

774
00:39:17,730 --> 00:39:19,023
You should leave now.

775
00:39:19,106 --> 00:39:20,358
[Natalie] I'm not leaving.

776
00:39:20,608 --> 00:39:22,985
Who knows what that woman might do to you?

777
00:39:23,778 --> 00:39:25,237
It's okay, Mr. Mayor.

778
00:39:25,571 --> 00:39:26,906
I'll leave.

779
00:39:26,989 --> 00:39:30,493
I don't want to discuss important matters

780
00:39:30,576 --> 00:39:32,953
in front of insignificant people.

781
00:39:33,329 --> 00:39:34,663
-Bye.
-No, no, no, Miss Aguas.

782
00:39:34,747 --> 00:39:35,790
-Uh, Natalie…
-It's okay.

783
00:39:35,873 --> 00:39:37,708
No, no, no, no. Natalie is about to leave.

784
00:39:37,792 --> 00:39:39,168
-Are you sure?
-Natalie.

785
00:39:39,251 --> 00:39:40,419
She's about to leave.

786
00:39:40,503 --> 00:39:43,255
Natalie, I'm the mayor of this town, okay?

787
00:39:43,339 --> 00:39:45,633
I have responsibilities to take care of.

788
00:39:45,716 --> 00:39:46,967
And as my girlfriend,

789
00:39:47,051 --> 00:39:49,428
I'm sure you understand and respect that.

790
00:39:49,512 --> 00:39:50,554
Right?

791
00:39:51,389 --> 00:39:52,390
Okay?

792
00:39:53,057 --> 00:39:56,560
[tense music playing]

793
00:39:56,644 --> 00:39:57,686
Okay.

794
00:39:58,312 --> 00:40:00,106
For you, I'll go.

795
00:40:00,940 --> 00:40:01,941
[Arnaldo] Thank you.

796
00:40:13,202 --> 00:40:15,579
I am sorry about that, but, ah…

797
00:40:15,663 --> 00:40:16,956
Such a brat!

798
00:40:17,915 --> 00:40:19,792
I know. But I must say…

799
00:40:20,251 --> 00:40:22,878
you made me lie again, Miss Aguas.

800
00:40:23,462 --> 00:40:24,547
Really?

801
00:40:24,672 --> 00:40:26,132
I don't think so.

802
00:40:26,340 --> 00:40:29,802
I mean, who kept texting me,

803
00:40:29,885 --> 00:40:33,305
telling me he wanted to see me?

804
00:40:34,890 --> 00:40:36,934
Why did you want to see me, Mr. Mayor?

805
00:40:37,977 --> 00:40:38,978
Okay.

806
00:40:39,937 --> 00:40:41,564
I want to be a senator.

807
00:40:44,108 --> 00:40:45,276
And I need your help.

808
00:40:47,278 --> 00:40:48,279
What?

809
00:40:49,113 --> 00:40:50,948
You're going against Emilia?

810
00:40:52,116 --> 00:40:53,117
She's your mom.

811
00:40:53,200 --> 00:40:54,160
I know.

812
00:40:54,785 --> 00:40:57,079
But in our family,
it doesn't work that way.

813
00:40:57,746 --> 00:41:01,167
To us, men will always
be superior to women.

814
00:41:02,251 --> 00:41:04,211
It doesn't look like Emilia knows that.

815
00:41:04,795 --> 00:41:06,839
Okay, I'll get straight to the point.

816
00:41:07,465 --> 00:41:09,383
There are many reasons
why I don't want her

817
00:41:09,467 --> 00:41:10,843
to run in place of Grandpa.

818
00:41:11,010 --> 00:41:14,847
First of all, her stubborn
and reckless attitude

819
00:41:15,055 --> 00:41:16,515
will be our family's undoing.

820
00:41:16,974 --> 00:41:19,018
She will exhaust our money

821
00:41:19,101 --> 00:41:21,353
because I know for a fact
that she will lose.

822
00:41:21,437 --> 00:41:23,689
She will ruin our family's name,

823
00:41:23,772 --> 00:41:28,027
and I won't let her put all of
Grandpa's efforts to waste.

824
00:41:30,029 --> 00:41:32,531
Miss Aguas, I was born to lead.

825
00:41:33,532 --> 00:41:35,075
And this is my chance.

826
00:41:36,243 --> 00:41:37,453
I need your help.

827
00:41:38,537 --> 00:41:40,915
So, how can I help?

828
00:41:41,832 --> 00:41:43,125
I like that question.

829
00:41:44,418 --> 00:41:46,128
With the campaign funds…

830
00:41:46,921 --> 00:41:49,048
that you promised my grandfather.

831
00:41:50,716 --> 00:41:51,884
[chuckles]

832
00:41:56,055 --> 00:41:58,516
Well, I'll think about it, Mr. Mayor.

833
00:41:59,808 --> 00:42:01,435
Because to be honest…

834
00:42:02,228 --> 00:42:07,274
I'd rather support Emilia than you.

835
00:42:12,404 --> 00:42:14,073
What can I do to change your mind?

836
00:42:14,156 --> 00:42:18,994
[sultry music playing]

837
00:42:20,538 --> 00:42:22,581
The farmers' land…

838
00:42:23,749 --> 00:42:25,668
Aren't they in your name?

839
00:42:27,086 --> 00:42:28,087
I want it.

840
00:42:28,462 --> 00:42:29,755
Give it to me.

841
00:42:34,969 --> 00:42:38,097
Are you doing this
for the farmers or for Diego?

842
00:42:39,640 --> 00:42:41,308
Because I'll be honest with you.

843
00:42:41,392 --> 00:42:44,395
I'm jealous of the attention
you're giving my brother.

844
00:42:45,771 --> 00:42:48,190
Well, Mr. Mayor, it's not my fault

845
00:42:48,274 --> 00:42:50,109
if your brother moves…

846
00:42:50,693 --> 00:42:51,944
faster than you do.

847
00:42:52,528 --> 00:42:53,571
[scoffs]

848
00:42:54,863 --> 00:42:55,864
Okay.

849
00:42:56,740 --> 00:43:00,244
How many times do I have to tell you?

850
00:43:00,828 --> 00:43:02,580
I like you, Miss Aguas.

851
00:43:03,789 --> 00:43:05,165
I really like you.

852
00:43:05,958 --> 00:43:07,167
Mr. Mayor…

853
00:43:08,586 --> 00:43:10,087
I know that.

854
00:43:11,922 --> 00:43:13,048
But of course,

855
00:43:13,591 --> 00:43:16,051
I can't be yours because…

856
00:43:17,219 --> 00:43:18,929
you already have Natalie.

857
00:43:20,139 --> 00:43:24,226
And you can't win the prize…

858
00:43:29,064 --> 00:43:31,275
if you don't give me what I want.

859
00:43:31,442 --> 00:43:35,946
[tense music playing]

860
00:43:38,782 --> 00:43:40,284
[phone ringing]

861
00:43:41,410 --> 00:43:43,203
It's Emilia calling.

862
00:43:43,370 --> 00:43:45,205
-[phone ringing]
-I almost forgot.

863
00:43:45,623 --> 00:43:48,417
-We have a meeting for…
-[phone ringing]

864
00:43:49,460 --> 00:43:50,961
her senatorial bid.

865
00:43:58,844 --> 00:44:00,179
Bye, Mr. Mayor.

866
00:44:01,472 --> 00:44:06,018
[tense music playing]

867
00:44:12,941 --> 00:44:14,652
You have to give me what I want…

868
00:44:15,611 --> 00:44:17,363
before you get the prize.

869
00:44:27,956 --> 00:44:29,708
So, I just had to inform you

870
00:44:29,792 --> 00:44:32,878
that I found a new site
for the EPZ project.

871
00:44:33,337 --> 00:44:35,381
I'll have the team discuss it with you

872
00:44:35,464 --> 00:44:37,925
when your schedule permits it.

873
00:44:38,592 --> 00:44:40,886
I don't want to focus on that, Ivy.

874
00:44:41,345 --> 00:44:43,305
I want to focus on me.

875
00:44:44,390 --> 00:44:45,391
Okay.

876
00:44:45,808 --> 00:44:49,186
Where is the support you
promised my father's candidacy?

877
00:44:49,269 --> 00:44:51,271
Yes, I'm still supporting your father.

878
00:44:51,355 --> 00:44:53,482
Well then, I want you
to fulfill that promise.

879
00:44:53,565 --> 00:44:55,067
Where's the money? Give it to me.

880
00:44:56,693 --> 00:44:58,112
Emilia, relax.

881
00:44:59,154 --> 00:45:02,199
I said I'd support your father.

882
00:45:02,825 --> 00:45:03,784
Not you.

883
00:45:03,867 --> 00:45:06,161
Ivy, I'm replacing my father.

884
00:45:08,914 --> 00:45:10,666
I'm not so sure, Emilia.

885
00:45:10,916 --> 00:45:12,209
You see, that's…

886
00:45:13,001 --> 00:45:15,796
That's not what I heard
from your son, the Mayor.

887
00:45:18,173 --> 00:45:19,216
Tell me.

888
00:45:20,384 --> 00:45:21,677
Emilia…

889
00:45:23,011 --> 00:45:24,888
Yes, I'm your friend.

890
00:45:25,055 --> 00:45:27,224
But I don't want any trouble.

891
00:45:27,850 --> 00:45:28,976
Maybe…

892
00:45:29,476 --> 00:45:31,186
you should just ask your son.

893
00:45:31,979 --> 00:45:36,442
[tense music playing]

894
00:45:39,153 --> 00:45:43,574
[suspenseful music playing]

895
00:45:54,877 --> 00:45:58,755
TRANSFER CERTIFICATE OF TITLE
ARNALDO ARDIENTE TORILLO

896
00:45:59,965 --> 00:46:01,133
Arnaldo?

897
00:46:02,092 --> 00:46:03,177
What's that?

898
00:46:03,635 --> 00:46:04,803
Nothing.

899
00:46:04,887 --> 00:46:06,889
Just some files I had Grandpa sign before.

900
00:46:07,973 --> 00:46:08,891
See you, Mom.

901
00:46:08,974 --> 00:46:11,101
Are you sure? What's that
you're keeping from me?

902
00:46:13,187 --> 00:46:14,897
Nothing. I don't keep anything from you.

903
00:46:17,107 --> 00:46:19,985
Okay, because I don't like you
keeping secrets from me.

904
00:46:22,279 --> 00:46:25,949
[suspenseful music playing]

905
00:46:43,425 --> 00:46:47,095
[unsettling music playing]

906
00:46:48,847 --> 00:46:51,058
EPZ INVESTOR IVY AGUAS
FARMER'S HERO

907
00:46:55,354 --> 00:46:56,897
What newspaper is that, Auntie?

908
00:46:56,980 --> 00:46:59,358
The one from Ardiente.

909
00:46:59,816 --> 00:47:01,318
<i>It has a picture of…</i>

910
00:47:01,568 --> 00:47:02,736
a woman.

911
00:47:02,945 --> 00:47:05,197
Her name's Ivy Aguas.

912
00:47:05,781 --> 00:47:07,533
<i>She's really interested in it.</i>

913
00:47:07,950 --> 00:47:09,660
She keeps looking at it.

914
00:47:12,829 --> 00:47:14,248
Okay, here's what you should do.

915
00:47:14,581 --> 00:47:16,250
Observe her closely.

916
00:47:16,500 --> 00:47:20,128
If she says or does anything strange,

917
00:47:20,462 --> 00:47:21,838
call me right away.

918
00:47:22,965 --> 00:47:24,424
[Belen] <i>When will you be back?</i>

919
00:47:24,800 --> 00:47:26,051
I don't know yet.

920
00:47:26,677 --> 00:47:28,512
Emilia's watching my every move.

921
00:47:28,679 --> 00:47:29,680
All right.

922
00:47:29,763 --> 00:47:31,557
I'll keep an eye on her.

923
00:47:32,307 --> 00:47:35,394
[unsettling music playing]

924
00:47:40,941 --> 00:47:42,234
Who were you talking to, Raul?

925
00:47:42,401 --> 00:47:44,945
[dramatic music playing]

926
00:47:47,614 --> 00:47:51,285
[unsettling music playing]

927
00:48:10,679 --> 00:48:14,099
[unsettling music playing]

928
00:48:35,621 --> 00:48:42,461
[unsettling music playing]

929
00:48:58,935 --> 00:49:00,604
[Arnaldo] <i>I'm a man</i>
<i>of my word, Miss Aguas.</i>

930
00:49:00,687 --> 00:49:01,647
<i>I hope you are, too.</i>

931
00:49:01,730 --> 00:49:02,856
[Natalie] <i>You just won't stop</i>

932
00:49:02,939 --> 00:49:04,566
<i>flirting with my boyfriend, huh?</i>

933
00:49:04,650 --> 00:49:06,401
<i>Choose. Is it Ivy?</i>

934
00:49:06,485 --> 00:49:10,238
<i>Or my daddy's support</i>
<i>for your senatorial ambition.</i>

935
00:49:10,322 --> 00:49:12,032
[Emilia] <i>Well, I called this meeting</i>

936
00:49:12,115 --> 00:49:13,575
<i>to correct some mistakes.</i>

937
00:49:13,659 --> 00:49:14,743
<i>Arnaldo doesn't know</i>

938
00:49:14,826 --> 00:49:16,495
<i>that Dad already gave that to me,</i>

939
00:49:16,578 --> 00:49:18,455
<i>so I had it transferred under my name.</i>

940
00:49:18,538 --> 00:49:20,874
<i>Raul, you need to get back here right now.</i>

941
00:49:20,957 --> 00:49:22,292
[Raul] <i>Why? What happened to her?</i>

942
00:49:22,376 --> 00:49:24,419
<i>I think she's coming back to her senses.</i>

943
00:49:24,711 --> 00:49:25,837
[Ivy] <i>What are we doing here?</i>

944
00:49:25,921 --> 00:49:27,506
[Diego] <i>Didn't I say I'd bring you</i>

945
00:49:27,589 --> 00:49:29,633
<i>somewhere a little more peaceful?</i>

946
00:49:31,009 --> 00:49:31,968
[gunshot]

947
00:49:32,052 --> 00:49:34,805
[theme music playing]
